    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1086/722415",
      "sequence": 1,
      "source_sequence": 1109,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Partial Identification in Matching Models for the Marriage Market",
      "title_cn": "婚姻市场匹配模型的部分识别",
      "authors": [
        "Cristina Gualdani",
        "Shruti Sinha"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "We study partial identification of the preference parameters in the one-to-one matching model with perfectly transferable utilities. We do so without imposing parametric distributional assumptions on the unobserved heterogeneity and with data on one large market. We provide a tractable characterization of the identified set under various classes of nonparametric distributional assumptions on the unobserved heterogeneity. We reexamine some of the relevant questions in the empirical literature on the marriage market, which have been previously studied under the logit assumption. Our results reveal that many findings in the aforementioned literature are primarily driven by such parametric restrictions.",
      "abstract_cn": "我们研究了具有完全可转移效用的一对一匹配模型中偏好参数的部分识别问题。我们在不对未观测异质性施加参数分布假设的情况下，利用一个大型市场的数据进行分析。我们提供了在未观测异质性的各类非参数分布假设下识别集的可处理特征描述。我们重新审视了婚姻市场实证文献中的一些相关问题，这些问题此前在logit假设下被研究过。我们的结果表明，上述文献中的许多发现主要是由这类参数限制所驱动的。",
